    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d970">

                <pb facs="0942" n="844" xml:id="pg844"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Señor Oalderon.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-09-18"><hi rendition="#italic">September 18,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 4.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your telegram of yesterday’s date, advising the Department of the profound
                    sorrow felt by the Government, the people of Peru, and yourself, in view of the
                    disaster which has befallen the people of Texas.</p>
                <p>Your telegram has been communicated to the President, and I am charged by him to
                    express his sincere appreciation of the sympathetic message you have
                    conveyed.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
